('math-counting-principle-01','mathematics','algebra','Permutations and combinations','Counting principle','A student can choose one of 3 shirts and one of 4 trousers. How many outfits are possible?','["7","12","24","1"]',1,'By the multiplication principle, there are 3×4=12 outfits.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-permutations-repetition-01','mathematics','algebra','Permutations and combinations','Permutations with and without repetition','How many distinct arrangements of the letters in LEVEL are possible?','["120","60","30","20"]',2,'LEVEL has 5 letters with L repeated twice and E repeated twice, so 5!/(2!2!)=30.','standard',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-circular-permutations-01','mathematics','algebra','Permutations and combinations','Circular permutations','In how many ways can 6 distinct people sit around a circular table?','["720","120","60","36"]',1,'Rotations are identical in a circular arrangement, giving (6−1)!=120.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-restricted-arrangements-01','mathematics','algebra','Permutations and combinations','Restricted arrangements','How many arrangements of ABCD have A and B together?','["6","8","12","24"]',2,'Treat AB or BA as one block: 3! arrangements of the block,C,D, multiplied by 2 internal orders, gives 12.','standard',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-combinations-identities-01','mathematics','algebra','Permutations and combinations','Combinations and identities','What is ⁸C₂?','["16","28","56","64"]',1,'⁸C₂=8×7/(2×1)=28.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-binomial-positive-index-01','mathematics','algebra','Binomial theorem','Positive integral index','What is the coefficient of x² in (1+x)⁵?','["5","10","20","25"]',1,'The coefficient is ⁵C₂=10.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-binomial-general-term-01','mathematics','algebra','Binomial theorem','General and middle terms','The general term Tᵣ₊₁ in (a+b)ⁿ is:','["ⁿCᵣ aⁿ⁻ʳbʳ","ⁿCᵣ aʳbⁿ⁻ʳ","n(a+b)ʳ","ⁿPᵣ aⁿ⁻ʳbʳ"]',0,'The binomial theorem gives Tᵣ₊₁=ⁿCᵣaⁿ⁻ʳbʳ.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
