('math-induction-principle-01','mathematics','algebra','Mathematical induction','Principle of induction','After proving P(1), what must the induction step establish?','["P(k) implies P(k+1)","P(k+1) implies P(k)","P(1) implies P(k) directly","P(k) is false"]',0,'Mathematical induction requires showing that truth at an arbitrary k forces truth at k+1.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-induction-divisibility-01','mathematics','algebra','Mathematical induction','Divisibility proofs','Which expression is divisible by 3 for every positive integer n?','["4ⁿ−1","2ⁿ−1","3ⁿ+1","n²+1"]',0,'Since 4≡1 (mod 3), 4ⁿ−1≡0 (mod 3) for all positive n.','standard',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-induction-inequality-01','mathematics','algebra','Mathematical induction','Inequality proofs','Which inequality is valid for every integer n≥1?','["2ⁿ≥n+1","2ⁿ≤n","n²<n","n!<1"]',0,'The base case is equality at n=1, and doubling preserves a value at least one more than the next integer.','standard',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-partial-distinct-linear-01','mathematics','algebra','Partial fractions','Distinct linear factors','In A/(x−1)+B/(x+2), which denominators correspond to 1/((x−1)(x+2))?','["The two distinct linear factors","A repeated linear factor","An irreducible quadratic","No factorisation"]',0,'Each distinct linear factor contributes one constant-numerator fraction.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','State-board Intermediate Mathematics; official EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
('math-partial-repeated-linear-01','mathematics','algebra','Partial fractions','Repeated linear factors','Which terms are required for a factor (x−1)² in a partial-fraction decomposition?','["A/(x−1)+B/(x−1)²","A/(x−1)² only","(Ax+B)/(x−1)²","A(x−1)+B(x−1)²"]',0,'A repeated linear factor of multiplicity two requires terms for both powers 1 and 2.','standard',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','State-board Intermediate Mathematics; official EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
